Input: {"question": "Who is the creator of \"The Wilderness Years\"?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 0, "end": 138, "text": "Adrian Mole: The Wilderness Years Adrian Mole: The Wilderness Years is the fourth book in the Adrian Mole series, written by Sue Townsend."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 139, "end": 189, "text": "It focuses on the worries of the, now, adult Mole."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 190, "end": 238, "text": "The book was first published in 1993 by Methuen."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 239, "end": 314, "text": "It is set in 1991 to the first part of 1992 and Adrian is 23¾ years of age."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 315, "end": 412, "text": "The book covers the same themes as the first volumes and continues the regular format of a diary."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "start": 413, "end": 546, "text": "The book charts the progress of Adrian's wavering love life; he begins infatuated, as ever, with Pandora Braithwaite, with whom he is"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 0, "end": 63, "text": "series , from internationally bestselling author Sue Townsend ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 64, "end": 176, "text": "Once again she lets us delve into the hilarious and touching life of a character adored by millions everywhere ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 177, "end": 307, "text": "Adrian Mole has at last reached physical maturity , but he ca n't help roaming the pages of his diary like an untamed adolescent ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 308, "end": 447, "text": "Finally given the heave-ho by Pandora , he seeks solace in the arms of Bianca , a qualified hydraulic engineer masquerading as a waitress ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 448, "end": 513, "text": "Between his dishwashing job and completing his epic novel , 'Lo !"}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01", "start": 514, "end": 554, "text": "The Flat Hills of My Homeland ' , Adrian"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d02", "start": 0, "end": 259, "text": "of 8 Adrian Mole Language English ISBN-10 0413650103 ISBN-13 978-0413650108 Next slide of product details See all details Customers who viewed this item also viewed Page 1 of 1 Start again Page 1 of 1 Previous set of slides Adrian Mole collection 8 Books set."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d02", "start": 260, "end": 266, "text": "( J.K."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d02", "start": 267, "end": 309, "text": "Rowling Adrian Mole series collection set."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d02", "start": 310, "end": 530, "text": ") ( The secret diary of Adrian Mole aged 13 ¾, the Growing pains of Adrian Mole, True confessions of Adrian Albert Mole, Adrian Mole : the wilderness year, Adrian Mole the cappuccino year, the lost diaries of Adrian Mole"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 0, "end": 107, "text": "The Wilderness Years (Nick Lowe album) The Wilderness Years is a CD by British singer-songwriter Nick Lowe."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 108, "end": 154, "text": "It was released in 1991 in the United Kingdom."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 155, "end": 196, "text": "It was not released in the United States."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 197, "end": 464, "text": "The album contains material recorded following the demise of the band Brinsley Schwarz, which featured Lowe as the singer and bass player, and before the release of Lowe's first solo album, \"Jesus of Cool\" (titled \"Pure Pop for Now People\" in the U.S.) in early 1978."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 465, "end": 564, "text": "Three tracks were previously released on other albums, while others were issued on singles or EP's."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03", "start": 565, "end": 582, "text": "\"I Love My Label\""}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d04", "start": 0, "end": 382, "text": "Love , and Understanding `` `` So It Goes `` `` Halfway to Paradise `` `` I Love the Sound of Breaking Glass `` `` Cruel to Be Kind `` `` Switchboard Susan `` `` Without Love `` `` Ragin ' Eyes `` `` I Knew the Bride ( When She Used to Rock 'n ' Roll ) `` `` Indoor Fireworks `` `` The Beast in Me `` Compilations Basher : The Best of Nick Lowe The Wilderness Years Quiet Please ..."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d04", "start": 383, "end": 494, "text": "The New Best of Nick Lowe Related articles Discography Brinsley Schwarz Rockpile Seconds of Pleasure `` Teacher"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05", "start": 0, "end": 180, "text": "Winston Churchill: The Wilderness Years Winston Churchill: The Wilderness Years is an eight-part 1981 drama serial based on Winston Churchill's years in during the 1920s and 1930s."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05", "start": 181, "end": 301, "text": "It was made by Southern Television on a budget of £3¼ million and originally broadcast on ITV on Sunday nights at 10 pm."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05", "start": 302, "end": 395, "text": "It was written and directed by Ferdinand Fairfax, with historian Martin Gilbert as co-writer."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05", "start": 396, "end": 532, "text": "Churchill was played by Robert Hardy, who earned a BAFTA nomination for Best Actor and went on to play him in several other productions."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05", "start": 533, "end": 596, "text": "The series focuses on the decade from 1929 to 1939 during which"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d06", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "is the subject of the query ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d06", "start": 30, "end": 200, "text": "1 like Like Comment Clay Layfield 19 reviews 2 followers Follow Follow April 30 , 2019 A definite read for anyone wanting to grasp the genius that was Winston Churchill ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d06", "start": 201, "end": 341, "text": "While he is rightly remembered for his leadership during 1940-45 , it was only made possible because of his prophetic voice during 1933-39 ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d06", "start": 342, "end": 566, "text": "Many times Churchill was accused of politically bending to the wind ( changing parties twice ) , but this era of his life showed his determination to stand by principle and conviction when virtually every voice in government"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "Tauris ."}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 9, "end": 24, "text": "December 2011 ."}, "D8S3": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 25, "end": 155, "text": "Find this book : Anyone with even a passing interest in Winston Churchill will more than likely have heard of Sir Martin Gilbert ."}, "D8S4": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 156, "end": 302, "text": "As Churchill ’ s official biographer he has authored numerous works on the man , most notably the monumental eight volume biography of Churchill ."}, "D8S5": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 303, "end": 427, "text": "The Wilderness Years corresponds with the latter half of volume five , which is more positively subtitled Prophet of truth ."}, "D8S6": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07", "start": 428, "end": 562, "text": "Dealing roughly with the decade 1929 to 1939 , where we find Churchill , after his term as Chancellor of the Exchequer , a backbencher"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Sue Townsend", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00:c0", "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d01:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Nick Lowe", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d03:c0", "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d04:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "Ferdinand Fairfax", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C3", "answer": "Martin Gilbert", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d05:c1"]}, {"candidate_id": "C4", "answer": "Sir Martin Gilbert", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d07:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0307-0c80672a6b42:d00:c0", "entity": "Sue Townsend", "scope": "Creator of \"The Wilderness Years\"", "claim": "Adrian Mole: The Wilderness Years is the fourth book in the Adrian Mole series, written by Sue Townsend.", "answer": "Sue Townsend", "quote": "Adrian Mole: The Wilderness Years Adrian Mole: The Wilderness Years is the fourth book in the Adrian Mole series, written by Sue Townsend.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ra